#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:58
msgid "Version Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:60
msgid ""
"**p5.js 1.x** (1.11.3) is the default — stable, well-documented, broadest"
" library compatibility. Use this unless a project requires 2.x features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"**p5.js 2.x** (2.2+) adds: `async setup()` replacing `preload()`, "
"OKLCH/OKLAB color modes, `splineVertex()`, shader `.modify()` API, "
"variable fonts, `textToContours()`, pointer events. Required for "
"p5.brush. See `references/core-api.md` § p5.js 2.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:64
msgid "Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:66
msgid "Every project follows the same 6-stage path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:72
msgid ""
"**CONCEPT** — Articulate the creative vision: mood, color world, motion "
"vocabulary, what makes this unique"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:73
msgid ""
"**DESIGN** — Choose mode, canvas size, interaction model, color system, "
"export format. Map concept to technical decisions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"**CODE** — Write single HTML file with inline p5.js. Structure: globals →"
" `preload()` → `setup()` → `draw()` → helpers → classes → event handlers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:75
msgid ""
"**PREVIEW** — Open in browser, verify visual quality. Test at target "
"resolution. Check performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:76
msgid ""
"**EXPORT** — Capture output: `saveCanvas()` for PNG, `saveGif()` for GIF,"
" `saveFrames()` + ffmpeg for MP4, Puppeteer for headless batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/p5js_SKILL.md:77
msgid ""
"**VERIFY** — Does the output match the concept? Is it visually striking "
"at the intended display size? Would you frame it?"
msgstr ""

